window.docContents[235].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/VerifiedLibraries.Common.Spec.Curve25519/#file-VerifiedLibraries___Common___Spec___Curve25519":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/VerifiedLibraries/Common/Spec › Curve25519.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the computational proof and symbolic proof 12 headline theorems depend on it 145 of 258 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nDeclarations on this page (32)abbrev p25519abbrev edOrderLdef modPowLoopdef modPowdef fpAdddef fpSubdef fpNegdef fpMuldef fpSqdef fpPowdef fpInvdef sqrtM1def edDdef edD2structure EdPointstructure EdExtPointdef edZerodef edExtZerodef edExtOfAffinedef edExtToAffinedef edBasepointdef edExtAdddef edAdddef edNegdef edExtSmulLoopdef edSmuldef leBytesToNatdef natToLeBytesdef encodeEddef recoverXEvendef clampScalarBytesdef clampScalar\n\nCurve25519 Field $\\mathbb{F}_p$, Twisted Edwards Curve, and Point CodecComputable specification of prime-field arithmetic over $\\mathbb{F}_p$ ($p = 2^{255} - 19$), the twisted Edwards curve $-x^2 + y^2 \\equiv 1 + d x^2 y^2 \\pmod p$ in affine and extended coordinates (RFC 8032 Section 5.1), 32-byte little-endian point compression and decompression (decodeEdDalek and strict decodeEdRfc), and RFC 8032 scalar clamping.\n\n\n\nField $\\mathbb{F}_p$ ($p = 2^{255} - 19$) and Scalar Order $\\ell$\n\nabbrev p25519L27–28 ↗#Prime modulus $p = 2^{255} - 19$ of Curve25519.\n\nabbrev edOrderLL30–31 ↗#Prime order $\\ell = 2^{252} + 27742317777372353535851937790883648493$ of the Ed25519 basepoint subgroup.\n\ndef modPowLoopL33–40 ↗#Structural-recursion modular exponentiation (acc * base ^ exp) % m for up to fuel bits.\n\ndef modPowL42–44 ↗#Computable modular exponentiation base ^ exp % m (up to 256-bit exponents).\n\ndef fpAddL46–47 ↗#Field addition $(a + b) \\bmod p$.\n\ndef fpSubL49–50 ↗#Field subtraction $(a - b) \\bmod p$.\n\ndef fpNegL52–53 ↗#Field negation $(-a) \\bmod p$.\n\ndef fpMulL55–56 ↗#Field multiplication $(a \\cdot b) \\bmod p$.\n\ndef fpSqL58–59 ↗#Field squaring $a^2 \\bmod p$.\n\ndef fpPowL61–62 ↗#Field exponentiation $a^e \\bmod p$.\n\ndef fpInvL64–65 ↗#Field multiplicative inverse $a^{p - 2} \\bmod p$ (by Fermat's Little Theorem; maps $0 \\mapsto 0$).\n\ndef sqrtM1L67–69 ↗#Principal square root of $-1$ in $\\mathbb{F}_p$: $I = 2^{(p - 1) / 4} \\bmod p$ (RFC 8032 §5.1.3).\n\ndef edDL71–73 ↗#Twisted Edwards curve constant $d = -121665 / 121666 \\bmod p$ (RFC 8032 §5.1).\n\ndef edD2L75–77 ↗#$2 d \\bmod p$ used in extended twisted Edwards point addition (RFC 8032 §5.1.4).\n\nTwisted Edwards Curve $E(\\mathbb{F}_p)$: $-x^2 + y^2 \\equiv 1 + d x^2 y^2 \\pmod p$\n\nstructure EdPointL81–85 ↗#Affine point $(x, y) \\in \\mathbb{F}_p \\times \\mathbb{F}_p$ on the twisted Edwards curve.\n\nstructure EdExtPointL87–94 ↗#Homogeneous extended point $(X : Y : Z : T)$ with $x = X / Z$, $y = Y / Z$, $x y = T / Z$ (RFC 8032 §5.1.4).\n\ndef edZeroL96–97 ↗#Neutral element $\\mathcal{O} = (0, 1)$ of the twisted Edwards curve.\n\ndef edExtZeroL99–100 ↗#Extended neutral element $(0, 1, 1, 0)$.\n\ndef edExtOfAffineL102–106 ↗#Lift an affine point $P = (x, y)$ to extended coordinates $(x \\bmod p, y \\bmod p, 1, x y \\bmod p)$.\n\ndef edExtToAffineL108–111 ↗#Project an extended point $(X, Y, Z, T)$ to affine coordinates $(X Z^{-1} \\bmod p, Y Z^{-1} \\bmod p)$.\n\ndef edBasepointL113–116 ↗#Standard Ed25519 basepoint $B = (B_x, 4/5 \\bmod p)$ (RFC 8032 §5.1).\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 118–123): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesVerifiedLibraries.Common.edOnCurve\n\ndef edExtAddL125–136 ↗#Complete extended twisted Edwards point addition (RFC 8032 §5.1.4, 8 field multiplications, 0 inversions).\n\ndef edAddL138–149 ↗#Complete twisted Edwards affine point addition (RFC 8032 §5.1.4): $x_3 = (x_1 y_2 + y_1 x_2) / (1 + d x_1 x_2 y_1 y_2) \\bmod p$, $y_3 = (y_1 y_2 + x_1 x_2) / (1 - d x_1 x_2 y_1 y_2) \\bmod p$.\n\ndef edNegL151–153 ↗#Twisted Edwards point negation $-(x, y) = (-x \\bmod p, y \\bmod p)$.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 155–157): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesVerifiedLibraries.Common.edSub\n\ndef edExtSmulLoopL159–167 ↗#Structural-recursion double-and-add scalar multiplication loop acc + [n]P in extended coordinates for up to fuel bits.\n\ndef edSmulL169–171 ↗#Scalar multiplication $[n]P$ on the twisted Edwards curve (up to 256-bit scalars).\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 173–175): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesVerifiedLibraries.Common.isSmallOrder\n\nPoint Compression, Decompression, and Scalar Clamping\n\ndef leBytesToNatL179–181 ↗#Decode a little-endian byte list into a natural number $\\sum_{i} b_i \\cdot 256^i$.\n\ndef natToLeBytesL183–185 ↗#Encode a natural number n into len little-endian bytes (n mod 256^len).\n\ndef encodeEdL187–192 ↗#Compress an Edwards point $P = (x, y)$ to 32 little-endian bytes (RFC 8032 §5.1.2): low 255 bits encode $y \\bmod p$, bit 255 encodes $(x \\bmod p) \\bmod 2$.\n\ndef recoverXEvenL194–210 ↗#Recover the unique even square root $x \\in [0, p)$ (x % 2 = 0) of $u / v = (y^2 - 1) / (d y^2 + 1) \\pmod p$ via sqrt_ratio_i (RFC 8032 §5.1.3).\n\n2 declarations not shown (lines 212–245): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesVerifiedLibraries.Common.decodeEdDalek, VerifiedLibraries.Common.decodeEdRfc\n\ndef clampScalarBytesL247–252 ↗#Clamp a 32-byte little-endian scalar array per RFC 8032 §5.1.5 (curve25519_dalek::scalar::clamp_integer): clear bits $0, 1, 2$ of byte $0$, clear bit $7$ of byte $31$, and set bit $6$ of byte $31$.\n\ndef clampScalarL254–256 ↗#Clamped secret scalar integer $a \\in [2^{254}, 2^{255} - 8]$ from the first 32 bytes of SHA-512(seed).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/VerifiedLibraries/Common/Spec/Curve25519.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/VerifiedLibraries.Common.Spec.Curve25519/#file-VerifiedLibraries___Common___Spec___Curve25519"}});